# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js — glob, NOT a per-dir list. Tailwind v4 auto-detects its sources by
# walking the repo and skipping .gitignore'd paths, so ANY build dir missing from
# here gets scanned as source: its binary chunks yield garbage utility candidates
# (e.g. a mangled `pb-[env(safe-area-inset-bottom)]`) that fail CSS parsing and
# 500 the dev server. Every per-chat NEXT_DIST_DIR must match this pattern.
/.next*/
/out/

# playwright — only the linux baselines are committed. They are generated by the
# ubuntu runner (Actions → "Update visual baselines") and are what CI gates on.
# A darwin set is per-machine: two Macs both write __screenshots__/darwin/, and a
# 400KB PNG conflict is unresolvable, so it stays local. See playwright.config.ts.
/tests/visual/__screenshots__/darwin/
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/blob-report/
/playwright/.cache/
# isolated tsconfig Next mutates during the test build (keeps app tsconfig clean)
/tsconfig.pw.json

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Claude session files (but keep the shared skills + permissions, which every
# desktop working on this repo should get from the repo rather than re-approve)
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/settings.json

# Convex agent skills — generated by `npx convex ai-files install`, not authored.
# .claude/skills/convex* are SYMLINKS into .agents/skills/, which is ignored, so
# committing them ships dangling links to every fresh clone (6 were tracked that
# way). No trailing slash: git sees a symlink as a file, not a directory.
# Run `npx convex ai-files install` on each machine to materialise them.
.agents/skills/
.claude/skills/convex*

# Playwright MCP scratch artifacts (snapshots, console logs)
.playwright-mcp/
# references/ — the PDFs and the full-text .md conversions of them are
# copyrighted and large (vettox3 alone is 5.4MB / 159k lines). Only the DERIVED
# files ship: extraction notes, chapter indexes, gap analyses, citations.
#
# This is an allowlist on purpose. It used to deny by exact filename, and a
# second copy of each book sitting here under its original download name
# ("… (VetBooks.ir).md") matched nothing and was one `git add -A` from being
# committed. Denying by name only works if you remember every name.
references/*
!references/*-notes.md
!references/*-index.md
!references/*-gap-analysis.md
!references/CITATIONS.md
